# Copy to .env for local runs, or point a systemd EnvironmentFile at a copy.
# .env is gitignored; this file is tracked and documents the variable names only.
# It must never carry a real value.

# The one credential the stack needs. Every upstream call is made with it, by the
# router; nothing above it holds a provider key of its own. That included a
# second harness, which no longer exists — see
# docs/decisions/retiring-the-second-harness.md.
# Obtain one at https://portal.neuralwatt.com
NEURALWATT_API_KEY=

# Who may ask, as label:token pairs separated by commas. Absent means nobody:
# every request to /v1 is refused, which is noisy and safe. The mistake this
# guards against is an empty list read as "checking is off", which would put an
# unmetered proxy to a paid provider on the internet.
#
# A token is a bearer credential. Generate one per caller with something like
# `openssl rand -base64 32` and treat it the way you would treat a password.
WATTROUTER_TOKENS=

# Address the router binds. Loopback by default. Since #533 the endpoints are
# authenticated, so binding wider is a deployment decision rather than a
# mistake -- which it was when nothing checked who was calling.
WATTROUTER_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8080

# Directory holding the bge-small ONNX model. Shared with zeromem so the ~130MB
# download happens once. Leave unset to use the default shown here.
WATTROUTER_MODEL_CACHE=$HOME/.hermes/memory/zeromem-models

# Which embedder scores prompts: hash or onnx. Hashing unless set, because ONNX
# needs the download above and a first run should not be surprised by it.
#
# The choice is not cosmetic. A scoring head is only readable by the embedder
# that produced its training vectors, and the head is checked against it at
# load — so changing this means refitting the head. Hashing is also known not to
# separate difficulty well (see router/src/bin/train-head.rs), so a scored
# router wants onnx. Asking for onnx from a binary built without the feature
# refuses at startup rather than quietly hashing.
# WATTROUTER_EMBEDDER=onnx

# Where requests go. The provider's API by default; anything OpenAI-shaped works,
# which is what makes a local proxy or a recording one possible without a build.
# WATTROUTER_UPSTREAM=https://api.neuralwatt.com/v1

# The scoring head. Defaults to head.json inside the model cache above. Absent is
# not an error — the policy has a path for an unscored request — so a wrong path
# here is a router that quietly stops scoring rather than one that refuses.
# WATTROUTER_HEAD=

# One tier's model, overriding the default in router/src/tier.rs:
# WATTROUTER_MODEL_<TIER> for heavy, code, long, mid, cheap and aux. The table in
# README.md is those defaults, not a guarantee.
# WATTROUTER_MODEL_MID=qwen3.6-35b-fast

# Where each tier's model runs: WATTROUTER_BACKEND_<TIER>, one per tier, set to
# local or remote. Remote unless set, which is the board's answer for all six —
# every model is behind the upstream API. An unrecognised value refuses to start
# rather than falling back to remote, so a typo cannot quietly send work off the
# machine. The phone sets these the other way: local everywhere except the tier
# holding work no local context window can serve.
# WATTROUTER_BACKEND_CODE=remote

# Hermes state: config, plugins, memory database, skills.
HERMES_HOME=$HOME/.hermes
